<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="502d6389">&lt;p&gt;
    The Cost and Benefits Calculation Model includes calculations and summaries of&amp;nbsp;financial indicators&amp;nbsp;for the
    anticipated improvement initiatives taking into account the timeframe of the benefits realization and required
    investments. The model contains a detailed breakdown of planned benefits (increased sales or margin, reduced costs,
    etc.), investments needed to achieve those benefits, and projected future operating costs compared to the baseline
    operating costs.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="a56fe8a2"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="3792f70c">Cost estimates should cover all costs associated with the anticipated improvement initiatives, including human resources,
required physical assets and funding. Costs should be separated into capital and operating expenditure. Based on the
detailed breakdown of the projected benefits, capital and operating expenditure, key financial metrics (NPV, ROI, IRR,
Payback, etc.) are calculated. It can be beneficial to calculate an optimistic, a pessimistic, and a most likely scenario.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="94c64f9f"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="87ae84d8">To estimate financial impact of the improvement opportunity realization and provide stakeholders with the key financial
metrics to support decision making process.</attribute>
